# 02 Client Rules

## Stack and Entry

- Stack: React + TypeScript + Vite + Apollo Client + antd + i18next.
- Entry flow is `src/main.tsx` with `BrowserRouter` + `ApolloProvider` + app root.
- App shell and routes live in `src/app/`.

## Directory Conventions

- `src/app/`: app-level composition (`App.tsx`, `routes.tsx`, `theme.ts`).
- `src/features/`: feature modules (e.g., layout), each with explicit exports.
- `src/pages/`: route pages (current auth pages under `pages/auth`, home under `pages/home`).
- `src/lib/`: infrastructure adapters (apollo, auth token helpers, i18n setup).
- `src/shared/`: reusable hooks/utilities across features.
- `src/graphql/operations`: authored GraphQL operations.
- `src/graphql/__generated__`: generated artifacts (do not manually hand-edit generated files).
- `src/locales`: i18n dictionaries (`zh-CN.json`, `en.json`).

## Frontend Implementation Rules

- Use path alias `@/` (configured in Vite/TS).
- Keep route guards and routing policy centralized in `src/app/routes.tsx`.
- For auth UX, keep login/register consistency under `pages/auth`.
- Reuse antd theme tokens through existing `ConfigProvider` setup.
- For static modal/message/notification APIs, prefer context-aware usage via antd `App.useApp()` within provider scope.
- New folders/files and naming must follow `06-naming-and-placement.mdc`.
- Structural adjustments must follow `07-architecture-change-governance.mdc`.

## React Compiler (babel-plugin-react-compiler)

- The project has React Compiler enabled (`babel-plugin-react-compiler` in `vite.config.ts`).
- React Compiler auto-memoizes components, values, and callbacks at build time.
- **Do NOT** use `React.memo`, `useMemo`, or `useCallback` for memoization purposes — the compiler handles this.
- Plain functions and object literals are fine; the compiler will memoize them when beneficial.
- `useState`, `useEffect`, `useRef`, `useContext`, and other non-memoization hooks remain necessary.

## Styling Rules

- Current styling baseline: antd + component/page CSS + targeted inline style.
- Do not introduce Tailwind unless explicitly requested as an architecture change.
- Keep page-scoped visual effects in page-local CSS (e.g., `auth.css`) and avoid leaking global selectors.

## i18n Rules

- Any new user-visible text must be added to both locale files.
- Keep key namespaces coherent (`common`, `nav`, `auth`, `home`, ...).
- Do not hardcode UI strings when translation keys already exist.

